# N14 S5 finding (2026-10-04): the real root needs the sandbox's own userns
#
# Symptom: after T2 made the real root unconditional, `tests/security/
# test_worker_nonroot.py` (E5.1: the non-root worker shape) failed its chroot
# case with `FAIL rootfs sandbox: exit=-1`, while the plain and network
# sandboxes kept passing.
#
# Reproduced in the probe's own container (`--privileged`,
# `seccomp=unconfined`, `docker cp` rootfs, `setpriv --reuid 65534`), with the
# fork's own breadcrumbs turned on (`SANLOCK_REALROOT_TRACE`):
#
#   $ python -c 'build the image-rootfs executor and run /bin/echo'
#   result: Result(success=False, exit_code=-1, error='sandlock_create failed',
#                  reason=None, signal=-1)
#
#   $ cat trace.log
#   step: real_root: begin
#   FAILURE: unshare(CLONE_NEWNS): Operation not permitted (os error 1)
#   FAILURE: sandlock child: real root: unshare(CLONE_NEWNS): Operation not
#            permitted (os error 1): Operation not permitted (os error 1)
#
# Cause: the fork skips the sandbox's user namespace when the sandbox's
# requested identity already equals the mediator's (`context.rs`, step 5). In
# that shape the child is an ordinary unprivileged process, and
# `unshare(CLONE_NEWNS)` needs CAP_SYS_ADMIN in the *current* user namespace --
# so the real root cannot be built at all. The emulated root needed no
# namespace, which is why this case passed before T2.
#
# The one unprivileged lever that does create the namespace is the per-sandbox
# PID namespace: its intermediate process runs `unshare(CLONE_NEWUSER)` and
# writes the map before the final fork (`--pid-ns`, the retelling in N45's
# open-issues row). Both production manifests run it (`E2B_PID_NS=true`), as
# does the minimal compose stack, so the probe was the only shape building a
# mediated sandbox *without* it.
#
# Fix (this same run): `tests/security/worker_nonroot_probe.py::_executor`
# passes `pid_ns=True`, i.e. the probe now builds the shape production builds.
#
#   $ pytest tests/security/test_worker_nonroot.py -q   (x86_64 production-shaped
#     container, shipped seccomp profile, E2B_REAL_ROOT=1)
#   2 passed in 17.25s
#
# And the shape-sensitive set in the same container (x86-security.sh's legs, the
# 0 arm retired):
#
#   $ pytest tests/security/test_worker_nonroot.py
#            tests/security/test_pure_root_errno_contract.py
#            tests/security/test_uid_isolation.py
#            tests/security/test_real_root_denials.py
#            tests/security/test_chroot_exec_shebang.py
#            tests/security/test_real_root_mounts.py
#            tests/security/test_sandlock_isolation.py
#            tests/security/test_ioctl_inventory.py
#            tests/security/test_socket_families.py
#            tests/security/test_process_limits.py -q
#   37 passed in 330.16s
#
# Same container, the full `tests/security`: the remaining failures are
# environmental, not shape -- `python-mcp:3.14` is not in the local image cache
# and the registry mirror at 127.0.0.1:5080 is not running, so every case that
# creates a 3.14 sandbox answers 428 `warm_required` / registry 401.
